Description: EDITION ONLY: say the switch to software decoding, and keep an explicit refusal of it
 .
 Patch 0059 lets the automatic stereo filter ask for software decoding when a
 3D packing must be rearranged in system memory and copying hardware frames
 back is not allowed. The switch was told only in mpv's log at info level, so
 the person did not know the decoding path had changed (ORDER 343, row U33;
 Daniel, 2026-11-01: "either it works or not and the user must know").
 .
 The switch is now told on the OSD, the player's own way of telling the
 person, for eight seconds, and as a warning in the log, which mpv also uses
 when it falls back after announcing hardware decoding (force_fallback). The
 words are libmedia-gpu-route's (media_gpu_route_copy_back_off_text, 0.2.2),
 in the person's language among the edition's nine, and say how to copy the
 pictures back instead: Copy decoded video back on the Graphics page, or a
 copying decoder in the player. The decoding mode stays readable as
 hwdec-current.
 .
 mpv's own choice for refusing software decoding as a fallback,
 --hwdec-software-fallback=no, is now kept here too: hardware decoding stays
 and its pictures are copied back for the conversion, as with a decoder the
 person chose.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-02
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
--- a/video/decode/vd_lavc.c
+++ b/video/decode/vd_lavc.c
@@ -521,6 +521,18 @@
 #endif
 }
 
+// What the person is told when a conversion needs the pictures in memory and copying them back is not allowed:
+// libmedia-gpu-route's words, in the person's language, with how to allow copying back
+const char *software_frames_text(void)
+{
+#if HAVE_MEDIA_GPU_ROUTE
+    return media_gpu_route_copy_back_off_text();
+#else
+    return "Decoding in software: this video's conversion needs the decoded pictures in memory, "
+           "and copying them back from the GPU is off.";
+#endif
+}
+
 static void select_and_set_hwdec(struct mp_filter *vd)
 {
     vd_ffmpeg_ctx *ctx = vd->priv;
@@ -536,9 +548,9 @@
     char **hwdec_api = ctx->depth_software || ctx->software_frames ? NULL : ctx->hwdec_opts->hwdec_api;
     if (ctx->depth_software)
         MP_VERBOSE(vd, "Not using hardware decoding: the depth layer is decoded in software.\n");
+    // said where the person sees the player's messages, in their language (the player shows it on the OSD too)
     if (ctx->software_frames)
-        MP_INFO(vd, "Decoding in software: the filters need the pictures in memory, "
-                "and copying them back is not allowed.\n");
+        MP_WARN(vd, "%s\n", software_frames_text());
     ctx->hwdec_automatic = false;
     for (int i = 0; hwdec_api && hwdec_api[i]; i++) {
         bstr opt = bstr0(hwdec_api[i]);
@@ -1530,9 +1542,15 @@
         return CONTROL_TRUE;
     case VDCTRL_SOFTWARE_FRAMES:
         // A hardware decoder the person chose stays; so does copying back
-        // where the person or the machine's record allows it.
+        // where the person or the machine's record allows it, and hardware
+        // decoding where the person refused software decoding as a fallback
+        // (--hwdec-software-fallback=no, mpv's own choice for it).
+        if (ctx->use_hwdec && ctx->hwdec_automatic && !ctx->hwdec.copying &&
+            !copy_back_allowed() && ctx->hwdec_opts->software_fallback == INT_MAX)
+            MP_VERBOSE(vd, "Keeping hardware decoding and copying its pictures back: "
+                       "--hwdec-software-fallback=no.\n");
         if (ctx->use_hwdec && ctx->hwdec_automatic && !ctx->hwdec.copying &&
-            !copy_back_allowed())
+            !copy_back_allowed() && ctx->hwdec_opts->software_fallback != INT_MAX)
         {
             // not a failure of the hardware decoder: no fallback message
             ctx->software_frames = true;
